      "in_process_target_object_stale": true,
      "explanation": "The lifecycle worker loads cluster targets at startup and holds them in process. Its ConfigMap volume had already picked up 548b0e3c, but the running process still held 324dc5c4 from 2026-11-25T00:56Z, so it rendered the old digest into the showroom Application. The backend rollout (generation 382 -> 383 -> 384 -> 385) restarts only the backend pod and never touched this worker.",
      "why_this_is_not_a_pin_problem": "The live ConfigMap and the backend's mounted /etc/launchpad/clusters.yaml both carried 548b0e3c at the time of this observation, and the lifecycle worker's own mount did too. Only the worker's cached object was stale."
    },
